{
  "title": "About Table Plugin",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "48167500a2ce35f9",
      "text": "The **Table Plugin** puts a real table on a wiki page. Type CSV, TSV, a markdown pipe table or JSON into the item and it renders as a compact grid when it is narrow, or as stacked row cards when it is wide, so six columns still read in the panel. The \u2922 button opens the whole table as a sortable grid over the page. Double-click the item to edit its text."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "id": "f5402e22ed4afb21",
      "text": "CAPTION Boards on the bench\nBoard,RAM,Good for\nPi 4,4 GB,gadget mode and video\nPi 5,8 GB,the farm and Marvin\nPi Zero 2 W,512 MB,sensors"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "fa7e4b62da025aeb",
      "text": "Wide tables stack. Each row becomes a card headed by the key column, so the table below \u2014 the one that prompted this plugin \u2014 reads top to bottom instead of squeezing six columns into four hundred pixels.\n\nCards fold. By default a stacked card shows only its key cell; the \u25b8 arrow (or a click on the title) opens the rest of the row, and shift-click opens or closes every card at once. Put a [[Wiki Link]] in the key cell and the folded list becomes a table of contents \u2014 the link opens the row's page in the lineup, the arrow opens the row in place. The `fedwiki-table-stack` skill rewrites a table into that shape and writes the row pages."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "id": "683ab7f339a54b7f",
      "text": "CAPTION The ranked research strands\n| # | Strand | Time to evidence | Reversible | Needs | Judgement |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | [[Agent Score]] \u2014 a score read by a human, an agent and OSC | weeks: the tabletop tests it directly | yes | the ensemble | do first; it is what the build needs |\n| 2 | [[Musical Intention]] \u2014 minimum representation of an intention | weeks\u2013months | yes | reading + two embassies | second; the rain event is its first test case |\n| 3 | [[Improvisation Score]]s \u2014 event, graphic, text scores, conduction | reading only | yes | a library | run alongside 1 as reading |\n| 4 | [[Laban Notation]] \u2014 effort/flow/weight as gesture primitives | months, uncertain payoff | yes | a dance-literate reader | last; learn from it, do not adopt it |"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "66df428d966d3200",
      "text": "JSON works too: an array of row objects, an array of arrays with the header first, or an object with columns and rows."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "id": "5a3c574da20300ba",
      "text": "{\n  \"columns\": [\n    \"voice\",\n    \"role\",\n    \"instrument\"\n  ],\n  \"rows\": [\n    [\n      \"Marvin\",\n      \"host\",\n      \"speech\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Matt\",\n      \"reader\",\n      \"radio\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Laura\",\n      \"scribe\",\n      \"wiki\"\n    ]\n  ]\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "ec3accb6e0d97927",
      "text": "# Origins\n\nThis plugin is a clone of Ward Cunningham's [[JSON Plugin]] \u2014 the item owns its data, the server answers restful reads and api-key writes against the first such item on a page, and changes of configuration are journaled while pushed data is not. What is new is the rendering, the data interface, and the farm declaration that turns the same operations into REST routes and MCP tools."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "84927ba44540cef0",
      "text": "# DSL\n\nThe item text may begin with directive lines, one per line, uppercase keyword then value. Everything after them is the table.\n\n- **CAPTION** text \u2014 a heading over the table and the title of the enlarged view.\n- **LAYOUT** grid | stack | auto \u2014 force a grid, force row cards, or let width decide (grid up to three columns). Default auto.\n- **SORT** column [desc] \u2014 initial sort.\n- **KEY** column \u2014 which column heads each stacked card. Default: the first column that is not all numbers.\n- **FOLD** closed | open | none \u2014 stacked cards start folded to their key cell (default), start open, or draw no arrows and never fold.\n- **FIT** first | even \u2014 grid only. By default a grid sizes to its content and scrolls sideways inside the item. FIT makes it fill the panel exactly: *first* shrinks the first column to its widest cell and never wraps it, the rest sharing what is left; *even* gives every column an equal share. A bare FIT means first. A first column too wide to fit still scrolls rather than breaking the page.\n\nCells may hold [[Wiki Links]], external links in the wiki's square-bracket form, *italic* and **bold**. Nothing else is interpreted; HTML is escaped."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "378001d00d067134",
      "text": "A narrow grid that would otherwise scroll sideways, with **FIT** added. The first column sizes to its longest label and never wraps; the other two share the rest of the panel."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "id": "0d5f9d28651cb29d",
      "text": "CAPTION FIT first \u2014 the label column never wraps\nLAYOUT grid\nFIT\n\n| Directive | What it does | When to reach for it |\n|---|---|---|\n| FIT | fills the panel | a narrow table that almost fits |\n| LAYOUT | grid or cards | prose cells read better as cards |\n| KEY | heads each card | stack mode only |"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "059606d82c39ac7e",
      "text": "# Data Interface\n\nA rendered table item is a data source for the rest of the lineup.\n\n- It carries the class **table-source** and its DOM node answers **tableData()** with columns and rows \u2014 the house convention shared with the calendar-source of the [[Date Plugin]].\n- It also sets **item.data** (rows as objects keyed by column, numbers coerced) and **item.columns**, and carries the class **data**, so Ward's **wiki.getData** family \u2014 [[Bars Plugin]], [[Line Plugin]], [[Scatter Plugin]], [[Method Plugin]] \u2014 reads it like a [[Data Plugin]] item placed above them.\n- Hovering a header raises the same **thumb** event the data plugin uses for column highlighting."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "7662cc697684616c",
      "text": "# REST and MCP\n\nThe operations are declared in the package's api/openapi.json and mounted by the [[Farm Plugin]] under /system/api/table/ \u2014 the same declaration also becomes tools on the farm's MCP door at /system/api/mcp and a generated [[Table API]] page.\n\n- GET /system/api/table/read.json?slug=\u2026 \u2014 the first table on a page as columns, rows and records.\n- GET /system/api/table/list.json \u2014 every table on the site you asked at.\n- GET /system/api/table/csv.json?slug=\u2026 \u2014 the same as CSV.\n- POST /system/api/table/write.json?slug=\u2026&csv=\u2026 \u2014 push data, gated by the farm (owner login, private sites).\n\nFor json-plugin parity the plugin's own server answers GET /plugin/table/slug (append .csv for text/csv) and an api-key PUT for headless writers \u2014 see [[About Table API Keys]]."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "id": "6b12f31bf4db2ef0",
      "text": "curl http://<site>/plugin/table/<slug>\ncurl http://<site>/plugin/table/<slug>.csv\n\nprintf 'name,score\\namy,2\\nzed,10\\n' | curl -X PUT --data-binary @- \\\n  -H 'Content-Type: text/csv' \\\n  -H 'X-Api-Key: 35ece947aa90b581' \\\n  http://<site>/plugin/table/<slug>"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "00a125ce7edf3e41",
      "text": "Pushed data replaces what the item text says for columns and rows, but the text keeps supplying the caption and layout. The stats line under the table says how many rows and columns, whether the data was pushed, when, and how long between pushes."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "8ce1cd41ee1eacb2",
      "text": "# Repositories\n\n- [https://github.com/Hitchhikers-Guide-to-the-Galaxy/wiki-plugin-table wiki-plugin-table on GitHub]\n- [https://www.npmjs.com/package/wiki-plugin-table wiki-plugin-table on npm]\n- [https://github.com/WardCunningham/wiki-plugin-json wiki-plugin-json \u2014 the original]"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "0d404fb4f05be308",
      "text": "# See\n\n- [[About Table API Keys]]\n- [[About JSON Plugin]]\n- [[About Data Plugin]]\n- [[Farm Plugin]]\n- [[Table API]]"
    }
  ],
